<!-- SECTION 8: DOCUMENTS REQUIRED -->
<section class="content-section" id="documents-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Documents Required for Company Registration in Bangalore</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <ul><li><strong>PAN Card:</strong> Of each director and shareholder - mandatory identity proof.</li><li><strong>Aadhaar Card:</strong> Of each director - address verification for DIN application.</li><li><strong>Passport-Size Photograph:</strong> Recent colour photograph of each director.</li><li><strong>Address Proof:</strong> Bank statement or utility bill dated within 2 months for RoC verification.</li><li><strong>Registered Office Proof:</strong> Electricity bill or property tax receipt for Bangalore premises.</li><li><strong>Rental Agreement and NOC:</strong> Required if rented. Agreement should be registered under Karnataka Rent Control Act.</li><li><strong>Passport (Foreign Directors):</strong> Notarised and apostilled passport and address proof.</li><li><strong>Voter ID or Driving Licence:</strong> Alternate identity proof for directors.</li></ul>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:16px;"><p><strong>Bangalore-Specific Tip:</strong> Startups using co-working spaces in HSR Layout, Koramangala, or Whitefield must obtain a formal sub-lease agreement and NOC from the co-working operator. RoC Bangalore frequently queries shared-address registrations. A dedicated desk agreement strengthens the filing.</p></div>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

